"_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":45374,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Medical","examName":"JIPMER","q":"Which of the following is most basic in nature?","options":["$\\mathrm{NH}_3$","$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{NH}_2$","$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{NH}$","$\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{~N}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2$"],"answer":2,"solution":"Basicity of amines depends upon the availability of lone pair of nitrogen for donation. Electron releasing group like $-\\mathrm{CH}_3$ increases the basicity of amines by increasing electron density over nitrogen, which facilitate the donation of lone pair of electrons.\nElectron withdrawing groups like -Ph group withdraws electrons and thus, make amines less basic by decreasing electron density over nitrogen. Hence, the order of basic nature of the given amines is\n$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{NH}\\gt\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{~N}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2\\gt\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{NH}_2\\gt\\mathrm{NH}_3$\nThus, $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{NH}$ is most basic.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JIPMER 2012","_marksId":"66d585dba75f05ee8564fb57","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":45375,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Medical","examName":"JIPMER","q":"The correct order of basic strength of the following are\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjipmer%252FcWUpF6T6491TJAq5x28V7y25kSdoOIoLM2h87knyH_U.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjipmer%2FcWUpF6T6491TJAq5x28V7y25kSdoOIoLM2h87knyH_U.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjipmer%2FcWUpF6T6491TJAq5x28V7y25kSdoOIoLM2h87knyH_U.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["I > II > III > IV","IV > II > III > I","III > IV > II > I","III > II > IV > I"],"answer":3,"solution":"$\\because$ Electron releasing groups increases the basic nature while electron withdrawing group decreases the basis strength of amines.\nTherefore, correct order is III > II > IV > I.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JIPMER 2017","_marksId":"66d5863ba75f05ee8564fed3","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]}]}